  "reason": "Confirm sender account and devices for Teams camera/audio issue"
}

{
  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "Check laptop for warnings relevant to camera/mic"
}

{
  "outcome": "resolved",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry about the camera and sound trouble in Teams. These steps usually fix it. Please try them in order: 1) In Teams, go to Settings > Devices. Check that the right microphone, speaker and camera are picked. Docks and headsets add extra options, so it's easy to end up on the wrong one. 2) Check your laptop's mute key, and make sure the camera's privacy shutter is open. 3) Close any other apps that might be using your camera, like Zoom or browser tabs with video calls. 4) Unplug your headset or dock and plug it back in. 5) Close Teams completely: right-click its icon in the taskbar, choose Quit, then open it again. 6) In Windows Settings > Privacy & security, open Camera and then Microphone, and make sure Teams is allowed in both. 7) In Teams Settings > Devices, use 'Make a test call' to check your sound. If the problem keeps happening on every call after a restart, or Windows doesn't show your camera at all, reply to this ticket and we'll pass it to our hardware team. Also, are you using your laptop BL-LT-0107 for these calls? It hasn't connected to our network in about 12 days, so please connect it to the office network or VPN when you can.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7), Marketing, account active, not VIP. Reported a black Teams camera and others can't hear her. Assigned device BL-LT-0107 (Win 11) shows offline, with last check-in 12 days ago (warning: no check-in for 12 days), so I couldn't check it remotely. She may be using a different device, or the laptop isn't connecting to the corporate network or VPN. Sent her the KB-025 quick checks and fix steps (device selection, mute key/shutter, apps holding the camera, replug, fully quit Teams, Windows camera/mic privacy permissions, test call). Escalate if it happens on every call after a restart or Windows doesn't detect the camera (possible hardware fault). Also follow up on the device not checking in.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-025"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
